order: 6
---
short_label: XII.6
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Pyramids of the same height with polygonal bases are to one another as their bases.
----
proof:

Let there be pyramids of the same height with the polygonal bases {ABCDE} and {FGHKL} and vertices {M} and {N}.

I say that the base {ABCDE} is to the base {FGHKL} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN}.

Join {AC}, {AD}, {FH}, and {FK}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="400" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.6 diagram" src="propXII6.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The pentagonal pyramids are cut by the joins AC, AD (and FH, FK) into
    // triangular pyramids; XII.5 on each pair, compounded (V.18) and taken
    // ex aequali (V.22), carries the ratio of the bases up to the whole.
    //
    // Joyce's figure is kept; the joins AC, AD, FH, FK are held back until
    // the proof joins them. A polyhedron draws no highlight, so the solids
    // the prose names get transparent twins: the bases (ABC, ACD, ADE,
    // ABCD, FGH; ABCDE and FGHKL are Joyce's own faceless pentagons), the
    // apex edges MA..ME, NF..NL, and octagon wireframes. The triangular
    // pyramids ABCM, ACDM, ADEM, FGHN walk all six edges; an octagon cannot
    // walk all the edges of ABCDM (8) or ABCDEM, FGHKLN (10), so their
    // prose refs light pABCDM (all but CD), pABCDEM (base plus MD, ME) and
    // pFGHKLN (base plus NF, NG), while the slides light base and apex
    // edges in full (PYR_ABCD, PYR_M, PYR_N).
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): M (lineSlider), N and A..L
    // (planeSliders), all givens; nothing to defer.
    var ORIG  = ["M","A","B","C","D","E","Mpyr","N","F","G","H","K","L",
                 "Npyr","ABCDEdup","FGHKLdup"];
    var JOINS = ["AC","AD","FH","FK"];
    var EDGES = ["MA","MB","MC","MD","ME","NF","NG","NH","NK","NL"];
    var GIVEN = ORIG.concat(["ABCDE","FGHKL"]).concat(EDGES)
                    .concat(["pABCDEM","pFGHKLN"]);
    var FIG   = GIVEN.concat(JOINS).concat(["ABC","ACD","ADE","ABCD","FGH",
                 "ABCM","ACDM","ADEM","FGHN","pABCDM"]);
    var PYR_M    = ["ABCDE","MA","MB","MC","MD","ME"];
    var PYR_N    = ["FGHKL","NF","NG","NH","NK","NL"];
    var PYR_ABCD = ["ABCD","MA","MB","MC","MD"];
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XII.6",
        elements: [
            "origin;point;fixed;-10,250,0;0;0",
            "1X;point;fixed;242,250,-91;0;0",
            "1Y;point;fixed;-105,550,-120;0;0",
            "1Z;point;fixed;14,375,288;0;0",
            "floor;plane;3points;origin,1X,1Y;0;0;0;0",
            "M;point;lineSlider;origin,1Y,-10,-10,0",
            "A;point;planeSlider;floor,170,200,0",
            "B;point;planeSlider;floor,180,160,0",
            "C;point;planeSlider;floor,70,150,0",
            "D;point;planeSlider;floor,30,220,0",
            "E;point;planeSlider;floor,120,250,0",
            "ABCDE;polygon;pentagon;A,B,C,D,E;0;0;0;0",
            "Mpyr;polyhedron;pyramid;ABCDE,M;0;0;black;random",
            "MX;point;parallelogram;M,origin,1X;0;0",
            "MY;point;parallelogram;M,origin,1Y;0;0",
            "ceiling;plane;3points;M,MX,MY;0;0;0;0",
            "N;point;planeSlider;ceiling,270,40,0",
            "F;point;planeSlider;floor,320,300,0",
            "G;point;planeSlider;floor,400,250,0",
            "H;point;planeSlider;floor,330,190,0",
            "K;point;planeSlider;floor,270,190,0",
            "L;point;planeSlider;floor,250,220,0",
            "FGHKL;polygon;pentagon;F,G,H,K,L;0;0;0;0",
            "Npyr;polyhedron;pyramid;FGHKL,N;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "FH;line;connect;F,H",
            "FK;line;connect;F,K",
            "ABCDEdup;polygon;pentagon;A,B,C,D,E;0;0;0;random",
            "FGHKLdup;polygon;pentagon;F,G,H,K,L;0;0;0;random",
            // Transparent highlight targets: bases, apex edges, wireframes.
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "ACD;polygon;triangle;A,C,D;0;0;0;0",
            "ADE;polygon;triangle;A,D,E;0;0;0;0",
            "ABCD;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;0;0",
            "FGH;polygon;triangle;F,G,H;0;0;0;0",
            "MA;line;connect;M,A;0;0;0",
            "MB;line;connect;M,B;0;0;0",
            "MC;line;connect;M,C;0;0;0",
            "MD;line;connect;M,D;0;0;0",
            "ME;line;connect;M,E;0;0;0",
            "NF;line;connect;N,F;0;0;0",
            "NG;line;connect;N,G;0;0;0",
            "NH;line;connect;N,H;0;0;0",
            "NK;line;connect;N,K;0;0;0",
            "NL;line;connect;N,L;0;0;0",
            "ABCM;polygon;octagon;A,B,C,M,A,C,M,B;0;0;0;0",
            "ACDM;polygon;octagon;A,C,D,M,A,D,M,C;0;0;0;0",
            "ADEM;polygon;octagon;A,D,E,M,A,E,M,D;0;0;0;0",
            "FGHN;polygon;octagon;F,G,H,N,F,H,N,G;0;0;0;0",
            "pABCDM;polygon;octagon;M,A,D,M,C,B,A,B;0;0;0;0",
            "pABCDEM;polygon;octagon;E,A,B,C,D,E,M,D;0;0;0;0",
            "pFGHKLN;polygon;octagon;F,G,H,K,L,F,N,G;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        slides: [
            { text: "“Pyramids of the same height with polygonal bases are to one another as their bases.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: PYR_M.concat(PYR_N),
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.6" }] },
            { text: "Let there be pyramids of the same height with the polygonal bases {ABCDE} and {FGHKL} and vertices {M} and {N}.",
              highlighted: ["ABCDE","FGHKL","M","N"] },
            { text: "I say that the base {ABCDE} is to the base {FGHKL} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN}.",
              highlighted: PYR_M.concat(PYR_N) },
            { text: "Join {AC}, {AD}, {FH}, and {FK}.",
              visible: FIG,
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "AD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "FH", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "FK", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Since then {ABCM} and {ACDM} are two pyramids with triangular bases and equal height,",
              highlighted: ["ABCM","ACDM"] },
            { text: "therefore they are to one another as their bases.",
              highlighted: ["ABCM","ACDM","ABC","ACD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.5" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the base {ABC} is to the base {ACD} as the pyramid {ABCM} is to the pyramid {ACDM}.",
              highlighted: ["ABC","ACD","ABCM","ACDM"] },
            { text: "And, taken together, the base {ABCD} is to the base {ACD} as the pyramid {ABCDM|pABCDM} is to the pyramid {ACDM}.",
              highlighted: PYR_ABCD.concat(["ACD","ACDM"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "taken together", ref: "V.18" }] },
            { text: "But the base {ACD} is to the base {ADE} as the pyramid {ACDM} is to the pyramid {ADEM}.",
              highlighted: ["ACD","ADE","ACDM","ADEM"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.5" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, ex aequali, the base {ABCD} is to the base {ADE} as the pyramid {ABCDM|pABCDM} is to the pyramid {ADEM}.",
              highlighted: PYR_ABCD.concat(["ADE","ADEM"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "ex aequali", ref: "V.22" }] },
            { text: "And again, taken together, the base {ABCDE} is to the base {ADE} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {ADEM}.",
              highlighted: PYR_M.concat(["ADE","ADEM"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "taken together", ref: "V.18" }] },
            { text: "Similarly also it can be proved that the base {FGHKL} is to the base {FGH}",
              highlighted: ["FGHKL","FGH"] },
            { text: "as the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN} is to the pyramid {FGHN}.",
              highlighted: PYR_N.concat(["FGHN"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "taken together", ref: "V.18" }] },
            { text: "And, since {ADEM} and {FGHN} are two pyramids with triangular bases and equal heights,",
              highlighted: ["ADEM","FGHN"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {ADE} is to the base {FGH} as the pyramid {ADEM} is to the pyramid {FGHN}.",
              highlighted: ["ADE","FGH","ADEM","FGHN"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.5" }] },
            { text: "But the base {ADE} is to the base {ABCDE} as the pyramid {ADEM} is to the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM}.",
              highlighted: PYR_M.concat(["ADE","ADEM"]) },
            { text: "Therefore, ex aequali, the base {ABCDE} is to the base {FGH} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {FGHN}.",
              highlighted: PYR_M.concat(["FGH","FGHN"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "ex aequali", ref: "V.22" }] },
            { text: "But further the base {FGH} is to the base {FGHKL} as the pyramid {FGHN} is to the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN}.",
              highlighted: PYR_N.concat(["FGH","FGHN"]) },
            { text: "Therefore also, ex aequali, the base {ABCDE} is to the base {FGHKL} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN}.",
              highlighted: PYR_M.concat(PYR_N),
              justifications: [{ claim: "ex aequali", ref: "V.22" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, pyramids of the same height with polygonal bases are to one another as their bases.",
              highlighted: PYR_M.concat(PYR_N),
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XII.6") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "V.18":  "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV18/",
        "V.22":  "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV22/",
        "XII.5": "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII5/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Since then {ABCM} and {ACDM} are two pyramids with triangular bases and equal height, therefore they are to one another as their bases. Therefore the base {ABC} is to the base {ACD} as the pyramid {ABCM} is to the pyramid {ACDM}. And, taken together, the base {ABCD} is to the base {ACD} as the pyramid {ABCDM|pABCDM} is to the pyramid {ACDM}. [!just XII.5; V.18]

But the base {ACD} is to the base {ADE} as the pyramid {ACDM} is to the pyramid {ADEM}. [!just XII.5]

Therefore, *ex aequali,* the base {ABCD} is to the base {ADE} as the pyramid {ABCDM|pABCDM} is to the pyramid {ADEM}. [!just V.22]

And again, taken together, the base {ABCDE} is to the base {ADE} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {ADEM}. Similarly also it can be proved that the base {FGHKL} is to the base {FGH} as the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN} is to the pyramid {FGHN}. [!just V.18]

And, since {ADEM} and {FGHN} are two pyramids with triangular bases and equal heights, therefore the base {ADE} is to the base {FGH} as the pyramid {ADEM} is to the pyramid {FGHN}. [!just XII.5]

But the base {ADE} is to the base {ABCDE} as the pyramid {ADEM} is to the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM}. Therefore, *ex aequali,* the base {ABCDE} is to the base {FGH} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {FGHN}. [!just V.22]

But further the base {FGH} is to the base {FGHKL} as the pyramid {FGHN} is to the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN}. Therefore also, *ex aequali,* the base {ABCDE} is to the base {FGHKL} as the pyramid {ABCDEM|pABCDEM} is to the pyramid {FGHKLN|pFGHKLN}. [!just V.22]

Therefore, *pyramids of the same height with polygonal bases are to one another as their bases.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

It is important to notice that the bases of the pyramids under consideration need not be similar, indeed they may have different numbers of sides.

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition will be used in @XII.10 and @XII.11 which concern the volumes of cones and cylinders.
